# Tab panels (show one view)

Use PrimeNG **`p-tabs`** / **`p-tablist`** / **`p-tab`** / **`p-tabpanels`** / **`p-tabpanel`**. Reference: **Bookings** (`admin/src/app/pages/bookings/`), **Activity** side panel, **Users**, **Reports**.

Do not hand-roll a custom tab strip unless the product explicitly asks.

## Main content card: tabs + list table

**Reference:** `bookings.page.html`, `bookings-list-panel`, `booking-types-list-panel`, styles in `admin/src/assets/layout/_tabs.scss`.

### Markup

1. Wrap tabs in **`div.card.card--tabs-list`** (standard `.card` **2rem** padding stays — tabs and table share that inset).
2. **`p-table`** lives in the tab panel with **`styleClass="table-bordered"`**, column sort + `LIST_VIEW_KEYS` prefs (see `list-view-prefs.mdc`). Same width behavior as Clients / Projects: **full width of the padded card interior**, not edge-to-edge on the white card.
3. Tab panel child (e.g. `app-bookings-list-panel`): **`display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 0`** on `:host` so the table is not narrowed by the custom element.

```html
<div class="card card--tabs-list">
  <p-tabs [value]="activeTab()" (valueChange)="onTabChange($event)">
    <p-tablist>…</p-tablist>
    <p-tabpanels>
      <p-tabpanel value="…">
        <app-…-list-panel />
      </p-tabpanel>
    </p-tabpanels>
  </p-tabs>
</div>
```

### CSS (`_tabs.scss`)

- **`.card.card--tabs-list .p-tabpanels`** — `padding: 1rem 0 0` only (top gap under the tab rule).
- **`.card.card--tabs-list .p-tabpanel`** — `padding: 0` (removes PrimeNG’s extra horizontal inset so the table aligns with the tab labels).

### Do not

- **Negative horizontal margins** on tables (`-2rem`, `card-list-table-bleed`, etc.) to cancel card padding. Tables stay inside the card padding (user-confirmed: Bookings).
- Put filters **below** the tab strip when they belong on one tab only — see tab-strip filters below.

### Tab-strip filter (one tab)

When a filter applies to a single tab (e.g. Bookings → type), put it **inside `p-tablist`**, **far right**, inline with tab labels, **above** the grey tab rule. Page owns filter state + list prefs; panel takes `@input()` and reloads. Flex the tablist (`margin-left: auto` on the filter wrapper) — see `bookings.page.ts` styles.

## Side card (Activity, etc.)

1. **Panel:** **`.card.card--side.card--side-tabs`** (`_side-panels.scss`) so headerless “scroll whole card” rules do not swallow the tab strip.
2. **Layout CSS:** never set `display: flex` (or other `display`) on **all** `.p-tabpanel` hosts in `::ng-deep` — inactive panels use `[hidden]`; flex on every panel stacks them. Scope flex layout to **`.p-tabpanel.p-tabpanel-active`** only. Set **`.p-tablist { flex-shrink: 0 }`** in flex side cards.
3. **Rows in the list:** compact **`app-account-card` / `app-person-card` / `app-pipeline-card-card`** (or `app-record-card`) inside **`.side-panel-scroll`**, with `[pickerMode]="true"` and `[selected]` — not custom pick-row buttons.

## Global tab chrome

- Active ink bar: **4px** — `.p-tabs .p-tablist-active-bar` in `_tabs.scss`.